From af98e030ecc8cbd0f807a6db832704a7fd93c629 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taehyun Kim <dice.thkim@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 14:08:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/28] SCUMM: Give the hi-res text its own outline and shadow
 settings

drawSvfnGlyph() took a shadow colour and never used it, so a glyph from
the extended bitmap format came out flat. The TrueType paths did draw a
shadow, but only ever a three-copy drop at a fixed offset.

Underneath both sat the same wrong assumption: that _2byteShadow says
what the text should look like. It does not. It describes how the game's
own .fnt was drawn, and a translation that replaces the font has no
reason to keep that decoration.

Add a [shadow] section that overrides it -- none, drop, outline, stroke
or game -- along with the offset and the colour. It reaches every path:
the extended bitmap format, both TrueType paths, and the built-in
blitter. The shadow is laid down in full before the glyph body, and at
8bpp a weaker coverage value will not displace a stronger one, so an
outline cannot eat into the strokes it surrounds.
